DXSPIDER USER WEB - INSTALLATION
================================

This procedure installs DXWeb only. DXWeb Admin is optional and has a
separate installation guide in dxweb-admin/INSTALL.

Prerequisite: DXSpider and its standard dependencies are already installed.
The local DXSpider IntMsg listener must accept the #WEB transport on
127.0.0.1:27754 (or the address and port configured for this deployment).
Ensure that DXSpider has the matching Web.pm/#WEB protocol implementation.

The Git checkout must contain /spider/dxweb/app.pl, start.sh and public/.
The service definition is supplied as /spider/dxweb.service.

Install and start the service (run as root):

    cd /spider
    install -m 0644 dxweb.service /etc/systemd/system/dxweb.service
    systemctl daemon-reload
    systemctl enable --now dxweb.service

The service starts /spider/dxweb/start.sh from /spider/dxweb and uses:

    DXS_HOST=127.0.0.1
    DXS_PORT=27754
    HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
    HTTP_PORT=7380

Direct mode
-----------

The defaults expose DXWeb directly on TCP port 7380:

    HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
    HTTP_PORT=7380

Leave MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY unset (or set it to 0) when clients connect
directly to DXWeb.

Reverse-proxy mode
------------------

A tested Nginx layout keeps the public port unchanged and moves the
application listener to a loopback-only backend:

    public/Nginx :7380 -> DXWeb 127.0.0.1:7480

Configure DXWeb with:

    HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
    HTTP_PORT=7480
    MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1

Nginx must proxy WebSocket upgrades and replace, rather than trust,
client-supplied forwarding headers. For example:

    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

With MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1 the backend listener is a security boundary:
do not expose TCP 7480 directly to untrusted clients. Only the trusted
reverse proxy should be able to reach it.

Edit the unit and run systemctl daemon-reload if these defaults differ.
Do not run dxweb/install.pl against the same Git checkout: that installer
moves and copies entire trees and is intended for separate distributions.

Verify only this service:

    systemctl status dxweb.service --no-pager
    curl -i http://127.0.0.1:7380/healthz

When the DXSpider link is established, /healthz should return HTTP 200
and state=ready. A disconnected backend may return HTTP 503. Open the
browser UI and test anonymous reception, Login and registration.

DXWeb Admin does not need to be installed for DXWeb to operate.

Configuration diagrams (Spanish / English):
  /spider/dxweb/docs/DXWeb_Configuration_ES.png
  /spider/dxweb/docs/DXWeb_Configuration_EN.png
See /spider/dxweb/docs/README-nginx for the example reverse-proxy setup.
DXSpider WebCluster uses the IntMsg listener (normally 127.0.0.1:27754),
not the traditional DXSpider client/node listener.
